  "details": "At least it seems to -most- of the time. I want a root bone to control some movement, and root to end bones to control other movements, but if you choose to ignore transforms on a parent script it also affects the child scripts, or at least it seems to 90% of the time. Not sure if this is related to not being able to fully test physics in play mode, or its its own bug but I have 4 out of 100 attempts to do this work, and the rest freeze the child scripts in place.\nI'll update if I find out if its an interaction with values or something, but it is certainly not easy to work with currently.",
